The theoretical prediction for the $B_s^0ightarrow D_s^{*-}\mu^{+}
u_{\mu}$ decay rate's dependence on the momentum of the $D_s^{-}$ meson has been examined to determine the best-fit coefficient for a specific hadron form factor expansion. This study utilized two distinct hadron form factor assumptions and found that the rate's dependence on momentum could be described by first or second-order Taylor series expansions. Comparing these two expansions, we found that the difference in charm quark momentum up to 4 GeV is less than 3%. Additionally, we determined the best-fit coefficient for a $1/m_{D_s}^2$ suppression term and examined its impact on measurements of the $|V_{ub}|$ coefficient from $B^0ightarrow D^{*-}\mu^{+}
u_{\mu}$ decays. Suppressing this term or treating it as a parameter had a negligible effect on $|V_{ub}|$ estimates. However, we recommend treating the $B_s^0ightarrow D_s^{*-}\mu^{+}
u_{\mu}$ decay rate's $1/m_{D_s}^2$ suppression term as a parameter in calculations of $|V_{ub}|$ to ensure the precision of the result. Finally, we discussed the influence of different hadron form factor assumptions on the extraction of $|V_{ub}|$ from $B^0ightarrow D^{*-}\mu^{+}
u_{\mu}$ decays and proposed a method to reduce this uncertainty. This method involves measuring the $B_s^0ightarrow D_s^{*-}\mu^{+}
u_{\mu}$ decay rate's dependence on the momentum of the $D_s^{-}$ meson to better understand the hadron form factor's impact on the $B^0ightarrow D^{*-}\mu^{+}
u_{\mu}$ decay rate and hadron form factor assumptions. By doing so, we can ensure the precision of the $|V_{ub}|$ coefficient's result. This study was supported by the National Natural Science Foundation of China under grants U183040102 and U183040103. It was also supported by the Chinese Academy of Sciences under grant KJ064-F01, and the CAS/EMA Cooperation Project. Additionally, it was supported by the Key Research and Development Plan of Shaanxi Province under grant 2020GD-03, and the Key Research Project of the Education Department of
